    "body": "Just to be clear, Geoffrey Garen proposes that we remove the skip-when-determining-incumbent counter such that when computing the incumbent settings/global object we use the topmost script-having execution context if its non-null. If its null (say, a timer callback), then fallback to the top of the backup incumbent setting stack.",
