    "body": "> @dbates-wk unfortunately that does not work. Specifically, if script does dispatchEvent and an event listener is a built-in function, we want to use the backip incumbent setting stack when that function is called, right?\r\n> \r\n\r\nCould we handle this by special casing EventTarget.addEventListener() when the callback is a built-in function?\r\n\r\n> In the above testcase, why is \"skip-when-determining-incumbent counter > 0\" true for the script-having execution context of the sendMessageFromAToB function?\r\n\r\nNotice that skip-when-determining-incumbent counter is incremented before we invoke sendMessageFromAToB() as per the [prepare to run a callback algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#prepare-to-run-a-callback). skip-when-determining-incumbent counter > 0 when executing sendMessageFromAToB() because the script execution context for B.html was at the top of the JavaScript execution context stack when we evaluated (2) by the [prepare to run script algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#prepare-to-run-script).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
